WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.52
In part three, stage zero created the repository and installed the skills.

00:00:06.52 --> 00:00:12.22
In part four, five more stages do real work: the brief, the stack, the requirements,

00:00:12.22 --> 00:00:15.13
the detailed designs and the user journeys.

00:00:15.13 --> 00:00:18.80
Each one writes documents into the product repository,

00:00:18.80 --> 00:00:22.26
and each one checks its own work before it commits.

00:00:23.41 --> 00:00:25.90
One executor serves all five stages.

00:00:25.90 --> 00:00:31.73
It checks out the product repository, runs the stage's agent with the stage's skill,

00:00:31.73 --> 00:00:34.78
validates what the agent wrote, and commits.

00:00:35.13 --> 00:00:40.16
Each stage has a definition: the Greenlit skill it runs, the files it may write,

00:00:40.16 --> 00:00:45.25
the task it hands the agent, and the validator that decides whether the output is

00:00:45.25 --> 00:00:46.01
good enough.

00:00:47.16 --> 00:00:50.27
The worker still holds no GitHub credential.

00:00:50.27 --> 00:00:55.85
It downloads the repository as an archive through the API, fenced by the lease,

00:00:55.85 --> 00:01:00.09
and commits through the same keyed mutation stage zero uses.

00:01:00.44 --> 00:01:03.05
Nobody answers questions during a run.

00:01:03.05 --> 00:01:08.27
When a skill asks one, the agent answers it itself and appends the question,

00:01:08.27 --> 00:01:11.64
the answer and the rationale to the decision log.

00:01:11.64 --> 00:01:15.90
The executor copies each question and answer into the run log,

00:01:15.90 --> 00:01:19.00
so you can follow the agent's reasoning live.

00:01:19.35 --> 00:01:23.87
Only the stage's own documents and the decision log are committed.

00:01:23.87 --> 00:01:28.05
A file the agent changes anywhere else is logged and dropped,

00:01:28.05 --> 00:01:30.93
and the API refuses the same paths anyway.

00:01:32.08 --> 00:01:37.44
After the agent finishes, the executor compares the working copy with the checkout.

00:01:37.44 --> 00:01:42.87
Changed files under the stage's outputs are committed; anything else is ignored with

00:01:42.87 --> 00:01:43.51
a warning.

00:01:43.86 --> 00:01:49.10
The validators are plain functions that return every problem they find.

00:01:49.10 --> 00:01:54.12
The requirements validator checks that every L2 traces to a real L1,

00:01:54.12 --> 00:01:59.95
every L1 has an L2, every L2 has a Given, When, Then criterion, IDs are unique,

00:01:59.95 --> 00:02:04.60
and the words should, may and might appear only in quoted text.

00:02:04.95 --> 00:02:08.45
For now a scripted agent stands in for the model.

00:02:08.45 --> 00:02:14.17
It writes valid documents from the direction and from what earlier stages wrote.

00:02:14.17 --> 00:02:17.17
The real agent arrives with run isolation,

00:02:17.17 --> 00:02:20.46
so no model ever runs unsandboxed on a worker.

00:02:21.61 --> 00:02:25.06
Seventeen validator tests name each missing section,

00:02:25.06 --> 00:02:27.65
broken trace and uncovered requirement.

00:02:27.65 --> 00:02:33.22
Six executor tests cover the skill and tools, the decision log, a failed validation,

00:02:33.22 --> 00:02:38.39
ignored files, the stack choice, and a chain of stages building on each other.

00:02:38.39 --> 00:02:42.97
The backend gained fourteen tests for the archive and the path rules,

00:02:42.97 --> 00:02:47.68
and the Playwright pipeline now runs all five document stages for real.

00:02:48.83 --> 00:02:51.39
Here is the real app, with one worker.

00:02:51.39 --> 00:02:54.09
The Owner names the project and submits.

00:02:54.09 --> 00:02:56.38
Stage zero creates the repository.

00:02:56.38 --> 00:02:59.68
Then the document stages finish almost instantly,

00:02:59.68 --> 00:03:03.32
because the scripted agent has nothing to think about,

00:03:03.32 --> 00:03:07.43
while the stages still to come take a couple of seconds each.

00:03:07.43 --> 00:03:10.93
The direction completes, with every stage succeeded.

00:03:11.28 --> 00:03:13.84
The same view on a phone, in the dark theme.

00:03:14.99 --> 00:03:20.11
Five stages now write and validate real documents, log every decision,

00:03:20.11 --> 00:03:22.45
and commit only their own files.

00:03:22.45 --> 00:03:26.98
Next, stages two and three: the designs and the design system,

00:03:26.98 --> 00:03:28.67
through Magic Patterns.
